@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Mantur Cut terminal draft persistence
+
+## Behavior
+
+Draft checkpoints contain the original project revision, original document, full draft document, operations, session identity and timestamps. Stale, cancelled, failed, rejected and applied sessions retain their saved evidence while dropping the writable DraftEngine. A proposal retained on a terminal session is archival data; hydration does not publish it as an active proposal or acquire an editing run.
+
+The v1 reader accepts older checkpoints without an original document. It preserves that omission when archiving a stale checkpoint and rejects a supplied original document whose revision does not match the recorded base. It does not reconstruct missing historical operations or documents. Terminal records that older builds already reduced to counts remain incomplete.
+
+The initial checkpoint, later draft writes, review and terminal closure run in order within one bridge runtime. Cancellation waits for an in-flight initial checkpoint before persisting terminal status. A terminal transition archives the latest committed checkpoint. A tool result from an older in-memory draft cannot overwrite a newer or terminal session. Failure to save a terminal record leaves the previous durable checkpoint intact and returns an error. Once terminal persistence succeeds, the in-memory session closes before ledger finalization; a ledger write failure therefore cannot leave that session writable.
+
+This change does not bypass project revision checks, storage ownership, CAS or user approval. It does not replay unknown side effects, automatically rebase an expired draft, or recover missing content in an existing project. The persistence queue is process-local and does not replace server ownership checks.
+
+## Verification
+
+Run with Node 24 and the checkout's installed dependencies:
+
+```sh
+node --import tsx src/agent/external-draft-persistence.verify.ts
+node --import tsx server/plugins/mantur-terminal-draft.verify.ts
+node --import tsx src/agent/external-edit-session.verify.ts
+node --import tsx server/plugins/mantur-import-session.verify.ts
+node node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc -b
+```
+
+The terminal persistence regression launches separate writer and reader processes against the production JSON store and runtime parser. It covers changed-project stale closure, failed checkpoint writes, ledger failure after terminal persistence, stale hydration, terminal review rejection, inert force apply, cancelled/failed archival round trips and a held draft write racing with cancellation. The existing import regression uses synthetic files and real HTTP to verify approvals, concurrent changes, cancellation and unchanged source bytes.
+
+Before the fix, the stale-hydration assertion received an undefined checkpoint, and the held-write race ended with a cancelled session overwritten as drafting. The fix does not require altering a running editor or its existing files.
