--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -346,6 +346,9 @@ Codex app/CLI and Claude Code use the same session workflow:

 Approval in Codex or Claude controls whether the client may call a tool. OpenChatCut project approval is required only for `manual` sessions; `auto` sessions explicitly bypass that review. Either mode commits the applied operations atomically as one undo step.
 If an `auto` session becomes stale, it returns an error instead of falling back to manual approval; discard it and start a new session.
+
+In the Mantur integration, `import_asset` and `import_folder` read media from the current Agent project. Manual sessions require confirmation before reading local files. Imported assets enter the editing draft, so successive imports and edits retain the same session revision; review applies the assets with the other draft operations. Compatible originals are referenced in place and remain unchanged. Concurrent live edits still make the session stale.
+
 Only draft-safe project read/edit tools are exposed in these sessions. Generation, export, project deletion, and other immediate side-effect tools stay unavailable because a rejected proposal could not roll them back.

 ### Codex
@@ -375,6 +378,8 @@ approve it in OpenChatCut before reporting that the edit was applied.

 External agents invoke the same internal editing tools and `EditorCore` commands as the editor itself. There are no separate project formats that can drift apart, and the live timeline is not changed while an external draft is being prepared.

+Mantur Cut retains an edit session's last saved draft, operations and original project revision when the session becomes stale, cancelled or failed. These records remain evidence after reload; they cannot resume, rebase or apply a terminal session. New checkpoints also include the original project document. Missing content in older records is not reconstructed. See [terminal draft persistence](MANTUR-TERMINAL-DRAFT.md) for failure ordering and verification.
+
